      <Placemark>
        <name>A- | Old North Columbus</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<img src="https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3APRDMAUcx0IN8w6vEBbdOkV0lkdAV5dKCyHi97vTByPr1AICwAfv7VslIyG84eoxo9SjHfgITkL5sRuC8aXEJ3bmYpHIFPPDKJsy0_yL1kkskSm4ujJeMoXwGBzLfBoud23DJ3o08V0tkBk892E3DaUwoJL31p8tiaIeclCBoNwBnltWLzZdjidmW4WeGcoNpugNZ7wN0ZqJhLU7yoAtmh90YHECdEYfp0HRTMPuFPVgxbP4fORrDpTszGHCGOo?authuser=0&fife=s16383" height="200" width="auto" /><br><br>Old North Columbus<br><br>I used to live here, and am a fan of the area. It's situated between the Ohio State University, and Clintonville (An A grade suburb). It's within walking distance to Ohio State, but not so close where you deal with a lot of college parties. The area is good to rent to graduate students and young professionals. <br><br>Statistics and More Info From Niche:<br><br>https://www.niche.com/places-to-live/n/old-north-columbus-columbus-oh/<br><br>Analysis From Homes.com<br><br>https://www.homes.com/columbus-oh/neighborhood/old-north-columbus/]]></description>
